(Vox OS Core Utilities)
A text called "Program Version" is "0.1.10".

(Parse the flags now)
A flag called "wants help" is "--help" or "-h", it is a boolean.
A flag called "wants version" is "--version" or "-v", it is a boolean.
A text called "Program" is arguments's name.

If "wants help" then,
  Print "{Program} - mount filesystems",
  Print "Usage: {Program} [OPTION]... DEVICE MOUNTPOINT",
  Print "With no DEVICE or MOUNTPOINT, or when DEVICE or MOUNTPOINT is -, read standard input.",
  Print "\nOptions:",
  Print "  -h, --help   display this help and exit",
  Print "  -v, --version output version information and exit",
  Print "\nExamples:",
  Print "\t{Program} /dev/sda1 /mnt\tMount /dev/sda1 to /mnt",
  Print "\t{Program} - /mnt\tMount /dev/sda1 (assumed) to /mnt",
  Print "See https://github.com/vox-lang/vox for more information.",
  Exit 0.
  
Open a file for writing at "/dev/stderr" called stderr.

A text called device is arguments's first.
A text called 'mount path' is element 2 of arguments's raw.

Mount device at 'mount path' with type "ext4".
On error write "{Program}: Could not mount {device} at {mount path}\n" to stderr.